She must have spied on us to capture him.

00:17:07.770 --> 00:17:09.990
I'm following her on my global positioning system.

00:17:10.240 --> 00:17:13.540
Aviva, are the basilisk discs ready for the creature power suits?

00:17:15.370 --> 00:17:16.650
Danita's heading to a plane.

00:17:17.260 --> 00:17:19.960
At this point, the only way we're going to save Splashclaw

00:17:19.960 --> 00:17:21.960
is by speed walking on water.

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:26.000
Prepare the suspended animation beam, Davio.

00:17:26.200 --> 00:17:29.580
Time for me to design this lovely lizard into a hat.

00:17:32.330 --> 00:17:34.520
Guys, the discs are ready! Heads up, Jimmy!

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:40.420
Energize! Coming at you, crap bros!

00:17:42.490 --> 00:17:45.380
Alright! We've got the discs!

00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:48.180
Now we just need to find a basilisk!

00:17:49.120 --> 00:17:51.510
Oh, we lost Splashclaw!

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:54.800
And it took us forever to find him, huh?

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:01.460
Let's do nothing.

00:18:02.690 --> 00:18:03.430
Don't move, Martin.

00:18:05.300 --> 00:18:06.660
I'm with you, dude.

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:08.340
Tree branch pose.

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:10.820
Dead tree stump position.

00:18:11.020 --> 00:18:14.780
Let's let the basilisk lizard come to us.

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:23.360
Activate creature power suit.

00:18:25.430 --> 00:18:27.190
Activate creature power suit.

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:38.370
You ready to take a walk on the wet side, bro?

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:40.750
I'm with you, Basilisk buddy!

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:41.830
Whoa!

00:18:44.300 --> 00:18:48.640
You'll be much happier as a hat than some boring lizard in a tree.

00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:49.740
Trust me.

00:18:49.900 --> 00:18:55.060
How can you be sad when I'm going to be on the cover of every fashion magazine?

00:18:55.870 --> 00:18:59.970
Now, let's play with this fabulous iced tea fetching f-

00:19:04.640 --> 00:19:07.630
The Creature Rescue!

00:19:09.280 --> 00:19:13.000
If you have big feet, plus speed, plus air bubbles,

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:16.610
then you're running on water with basilisk power!

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:17.840
Woohoo!

00:19:19.180 --> 00:19:20.440
Awesome, it worked!

00:19:21.600 --> 00:19:23.240
It can take you anywhere in science.

00:19:23.580 --> 00:19:24.760
But they're running out of time!

00:19:25.480 --> 00:19:27.300
Guys, Amita's getting away!

00:19:27.730 --> 00:19:29.310
We've gotta catch up fast!

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:31.350
Let's kick it, dude!

00:19:32.300 --> 00:19:34.680
Saving the planet with creature power!

00:19:37.010 --> 00:19:39.090
Okay, water walking sun hat.

00:19:39.290 --> 00:19:42.860
Get me a nice tea and spawn it.

00:19:49.180 --> 00:19:59.930
So thirsty, this time put a sprig of mint in it.

00:20:02.680 --> 00:20:13.510
do this all day and after I win that contest in Paris we can catch her we run

00:20:13.510 --> 00:20:27.210
faster they run in bursts and then sink to the rocks we'll make a new plan

00:20:30.510 --> 00:20:32.020
Okay, what's the plan?

00:20:32.510 --> 00:20:34.520
I don't know. I thought you might have one.

00:20:35.270 --> 00:20:36.820
Okay, rest over.

00:20:37.270 --> 00:20:37.930
Let's go!

00:20:43.060 --> 00:20:47.920
Dabio, this lizard hat is the perfect launch for a new line of sun hats.

00:20:48.390 --> 00:20:52.010
We'll come back soon and snatch all the lizards in the rainforest, alright?

00:20:55.720 --> 00:20:57.300
Not if we can help it.

00:20:57.520 --> 00:20:59.400
Was that a crat?

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:02.320
Two Kratts, in fact. Don't worry.

00:21:02.800 --> 00:21:04.440
Splashclaw, we're gonna save you.

00:21:04.880 --> 00:21:07.080
Dabio, get rid of those overgrown lizards!

00:21:07.220 --> 00:21:12.400
Oh, no, catch me first!

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:15.590
Huh? How do the big lizards know me?

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:17.970
Don't listen to them! Get rid of them!

00:21:19.280 --> 00:21:22.010
Uh-oh! Yeah, catch a Martin first.

00:21:22.470 --> 00:21:24.610
What? Trust me on this one, bro.

00:21:34.190 --> 00:21:34.990
Game over, Danita.

00:21:35.490 --> 00:21:37.680
I got you, Lizard Man.

00:21:38.050 --> 00:21:39.830
I win, I win.

00:21:40.850 --> 00:21:43.670
Game over for you, Chris Krat.

00:21:44.490 --> 00:21:45.330
Chris, over here!

00:21:53.690 --> 00:21:59.970
And Splashclaw, the Basilisk is...

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:02.300
Back where he belongs, running free and in.

00:22:02.420 --> 00:22:05.650
It's too far!

00:22:05.890 --> 00:22:08.590
You can't run all the way back to land.

00:22:09.220 --> 00:22:09.660
Good.

00:22:09.980 --> 00:22:12.720
We'll just catch him in the net again so I can get to Paris.

00:22:13.680 --> 00:22:15.040
Can we be of any assistance?

00:22:17.820 --> 00:22:19.140
That's a good splash claw.

00:22:19.540 --> 00:22:20.560
Safe and sound.

00:22:21.040 --> 00:22:21.840
Thanks, Danita.

00:22:22.180 --> 00:22:25.290
Darby-o, always not fun seeing you.

00:22:26.450 --> 00:22:27.370
Yeah, fun.

00:22:27.800 --> 00:22:29.400
No, it wasn't.

00:22:32.040 --> 00:22:33.270
Um, Danita?

00:22:34.460 --> 00:22:34.800
What?

00:22:40.850 --> 00:22:43.260
Well, beautiful lizards and birds around the world

00:22:43.260 --> 00:22:44.640
can rest easy for a while.

00:22:45.840 --> 00:22:47.240
Ooh, pretty head.

00:22:47.690 --> 00:22:49.810
Let's get you home, Splashclaw.

00:22:51.160 --> 00:22:52.260
Mission accomplished.

00:22:52.540 --> 00:22:55.380
The basilisks are back living free and in the wild.

00:22:56.270 --> 00:22:58.090
I sure learned a lot about them today.

00:22:58.510 --> 00:22:59.970
It takes wide feet...

00:23:00.190 --> 00:23:03.490
Fringes, speed, and spinning feet to create water bubbles,

00:23:03.550 --> 00:23:05.190
allowing them to walk on water.

00:23:05.680 --> 00:23:07.260
They can also jump out of trees.

00:23:07.780 --> 00:23:09.620
And they're great swimmers, like me.

00:23:09.930 --> 00:23:11.890
And they're great climbers, like me.

00:23:12.090 --> 00:23:14.610
And they eat fruit and bugs, not like me.

00:23:16.880 --> 00:23:20.160
And basilisks are the ultimate water-walking lizards.

00:23:20.340 --> 00:23:24.000
I don't know about you, Chris, but I think it's time for a...

00:23:24.060 --> 00:23:25.320
walk on the wet side.

00:23:25.930 --> 00:23:28.100
Hey, that's my line. Not today.

00:23:28.810 --> 00:23:29.980
Ready, set...

00:23:33.430 --> 00:23:37.290
The basilisk lizard could be one of the coolest lizards of all time.

00:23:37.750 --> 00:23:43.560
Must be nice to be able to climb trees, swim underwater, and then run right across the top of it.

00:23:43.660 --> 00:23:44.540
I can climb trees.

00:23:44.560 --> 00:23:45.340
And I can swim underwater.

00:23:45.750 --> 00:23:48.270
But we both can't walk on water.

00:23:48.960 --> 00:23:51.460
Unless you have a boat pulling on water skis.

00:23:55.130 --> 00:23:58.430
The basilisk doesn't have water skis, but he has these feet.

00:23:58.880 --> 00:23:59.980
They create a lot of surface.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:04.450
area on the water, and then they get running. This basilisk will stand up, like

00:24:04.450 --> 00:24:13.030
this, run with these hind feet. These two basilisks, born in captivity, have never

00:24:13.030 --> 00:24:18.940
walked on water before. Can they do it? Now we're gonna start their training. The

00:24:18.940 --> 00:24:24.500
male basilisk is bigger, heavier, and has those cool crests and ridges all down

00:24:24.500 --> 00:24:29.100
its back. The female, she doesn't have any of the crests or ridges, and she's a

00:24:29.100 --> 00:24:29.980
lot smaller and larger.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:33.120
So what do you think? Will that make her the best water walker?

00:24:36.250 --> 00:24:38.340
Hey. Are you ready, bud?

00:24:39.210 --> 00:24:40.760
Guess not.

00:24:41.440 --> 00:24:44.380
Maybe they'll only water walk if a predator's around.

00:24:45.280 --> 00:24:46.540
Let's try a simulation.

00:24:48.600 --> 00:24:51.440
Basilisk, perch on a tree. He says he's a predator!

00:24:55.910 --> 00:24:57.070
That didn't work.

00:24:58.220 --> 00:24:59.860
You know, it is possible.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:01.400
since they were born in captivity,

00:25:01.640 --> 00:25:04.240
they might not be able to learn how to walk on water.

00:25:06.860 --> 00:25:07.720
Whoa! He's swimming!

00:25:08.180 --> 00:25:10.140
Oh, nice!

00:25:10.520 --> 00:25:11.780
That's some good swimming.

00:25:12.020 --> 00:25:13.960
Yeah! Basilisk style.

00:25:14.860 --> 00:25:17.210
Now your turn, go on, go catch on with him.

00:25:20.150 --> 00:25:22.610
A basilisk lizard is a great swimmer

00:25:22.610 --> 00:25:25.690
and can hold its breath for up to half an hour under water.

00:25:26.100 --> 00:25:26.460
Wow.

00:25:27.120 --> 00:25:29.980
This might take a while to teach these basilisks.

00:25:30.030 --> 00:25:31.150
to walk on water.

00:25:31.840 --> 00:25:34.220
Just like anything, they need to practice.

00:25:35.020 --> 00:25:35.780
Go for it.

00:25:36.790 --> 00:25:37.310
Get marks.

00:25:37.590 --> 00:25:38.030
Get set.

00:25:39.900 --> 00:25:40.400
Yes!

00:25:43.850 --> 00:25:44.150
Good job!

00:25:45.860 --> 00:25:47.140
Let's try the male basilisk.

00:25:47.350 --> 00:25:48.390
He's ready to go.

00:25:51.990 --> 00:25:53.130
He did it!

00:25:53.630 --> 00:25:54.150
Awesome.

00:25:54.410 --> 00:25:57.030
Walking on water with the basilisk lizard.

00:25:57.630 --> 00:25:58.870
See you on the creature trail.

